    },
    "message": "Add a service capacity diagnostic for toilets, water and meals\n\nservice_capacity_diagnostic compares each service's daily work\n(people x uses per day x minutes per use) with what its working units\ncan do in an assumed 16-hour window, and reports the units needed to\nstay within a 0.8 target load. Water and meal units count only where a\nstaff member with the service skill is in the facility's zone, since\nservice cannot start otherwise. Toilet uses follow the Cabinet Office\nplanning figure of 5 per day; water and meal uses are upper-bound\napproximations of the Scenario's own need coefficients.\n\nThe generator adds the diagnostic's warnings to draft previews without\nchanging the Scenario or blocking a start, and the CLI exposes it as\nservice-capacity-diagnostic. The planning assumptions are registered as\nASM-SERVICE-CAPACITY-PLANNING-V1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
